# Introduction
The goal of this project is to examine which factors are associated with Airbnb listing prices in New York City using multiple linear regression.

The dataset, obtained from Kaggle and originally published by Inside Airbnb, contains 16 variables and 48,895 observations describing Airbnb 
  listings in New York City during 2019. Price will serve as the response variable, with six predictors: neighborhood group, room type, 
calculated host listings count, availability throughout the year, minimum nights, and number of reviews.

The analysis will include data cleaning, exploratory data analysis, and data visualization to examine the variables and their relationships 
  with price. Multiple linear regression models will then be fitted and compared using variable selection methods. Finally, regression 
  diagnostics will be used to evaluate the selected model and interpret the relationships between the predictors and Airbnb listing prices.


