## 2.4 Unusual Values

Several numerical variables were examined to identify unusual or potentially invalid observations that could affect the regression analysis. Particular attention was given to listing prices and minimum-night requirements.  

#### Zero price listings 


```{r zero}
# Check zero and negative prices
sum(airbnb$price <= 0)

# Examine listings with zero prices
airbnb %>%
  filter(price == 0) %>%
  select(id, neighbourhood_group, room_type, price)
```

The dataset contained 11 listings with a price of $0. These observations were excluded because they do not represent a valid nightly rental price.  

#### Minimum-night requirements  

```{r min_unusual}
# Check unusually long minimum stays
sum(airbnb$minimum_nights > 30)

# Count minimum stays exceeding one year
sum(airbnb$minimum_nights > 365)

# Examine the largest minimum-night values
sort(unique(airbnb$minimum_nights), 
     decreasing = TRUE)[1:20]

# Summary of minimum nights above 30
summary(airbnb$minimum_nights[
  airbnb$minimum_nights > 30
])

# Examine observations exceeding 365 nights
airbnb %>%
  filter(minimum_nights > 365) %>%
  select(id, minimum_nights, price, room_type)
```

A total of 747 listings required more than 30 nights, while 14 listings required more than 365 nights. Since minimum stays exceeding one year are not relevant to this analysis, those 14 observations were excluded. Listings requiring more than 30 but no more than 365 nights were retained.

#### High listing prices  

Listing prices were examined to identify unusually expensive observations that could potentially influence the regression analysis.

```{r high_price}
# Count listings above $1,000
sum(airbnb$price > 1000)

# Examine the most expensive listings
airbnb %>%
  arrange(desc(price)) %>%
  select(id, price, neighbourhood_group, room_type) %>%
  head(20)

# Calculate price quantiles
quantile(
  airbnb$price,
  probs = c(0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 0.90, 0.95, 0.99, 1)
)
```

There were 239 listings priced above $1,000, representing approximately 0.49% of the dataset. The median listing price was $106, while the maximum was $10,000. These observations were retained because unusually high prices alone do not establish that a listing is invalid. Their potential influence on the regression model will be evaluated during regression diagnostics.

## 2.5 Examining Variable Categories and Ranges

#### Categorical Variables  
   
The categorical variables were examined to identify their unique categories and the number of observations in each category. The numerical variables were also summarized to understand their distributions and identify their minimum, median, and maximum values.

```{r categories}
# Check neighborhood groups

table(airbnb$neighbourhood_group)

# Check room types
table(airbnb$room_type)
```

The dataset contains five neighborhood groups and three room types. Manhattan and Brooklyn account for the largest number of listings, while entire homes/apartments and private rooms make up most of the available listings.

#### Numerical Variable Ranges  

```{r ranges}
# Check ranges of numerical variables
summary(airbnb[, c(
  "price",
  "calculated_host_listings_count",
  "availability_365",
  "minimum_nights",
  "number_of_reviews"
)])
```

The numerical variables have different ranges. Listing prices range from $0 to $10,000, minimum-night requirements range from 1 to 1,250 nights, and the number of reviews ranges from 0 to 629. Host listing counts range from 1 to 327, while availability ranges from 0 to 365 days.

## 2.6 Cleaned Dataset
```{r cleaned}
# Create cleaned dataset
airbnb_clean <- airbnb %>%
  filter(
    price > 0,
    minimum_nights <= 365
  ) %>%
  mutate(
    neighbourhood_group = as.factor(neighbourhood_group),
    room_type = as.factor(room_type)
  )

# Check dimensions
dim(airbnb_clean)

# Verify exclusions
nrow(airbnb) - nrow(airbnb_clean)

# Check missing values
colSums(is.na(airbnb_clean))

# Check missing values in regression variables
colSums(is.na(airbnb_clean[, c(
  "price",
  "neighbourhood_group",
  "room_type",
  "minimum_nights",
  "number_of_reviews",
  "calculated_host_listings_count",
  "availability_365"
)]))
```

